diff --git a/Documentation/hydrogenx-v10-audited-pissarro.rst b/Documentation/hydrogenx-v10-audited-pissarro.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..000000000000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/hydrogenx-v10-audited-pissarro.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,1239 @@
+HydrogenX v10 for pissarro / MT6877 / Linux 4.14
+=====================================================
+
+This document is installed by the patch so the kernel tree carries its own
+verification checklist.  It exists because a governor that compiles but does
+not appear in scaling_available_governors is a failed integration, not a tuning
+problem.  v10 treats visibility, default selection, and runtime self-checks as
+first-class requirements.
+
+Design rules
+------------
+
+1. hydrogenx must be built through CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_HYDROGENX, not by
+   blindly linking it whenever CONFIG_CPU_FREQ is enabled.  The governor uses
+   the dbs common core, so the Kconfig selection must also select the common
+   governor helpers.
+2. schedutil remains enabled.  v10 does not remove schedutil because schedutil is
+   the baseline for scheduler-provided utilization and for A/B comparison.
+3. the clean pissarro defconfigs select CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_HYDROGENX.
+   This makes a clean build boot into hydrogenx without init scripts.
+4. /sys/kernel/hydrogenx exposes global state.  If the governor sysfs tree is
+   absent but /sys/kernel/hydrogenx exists, cpufreq registration failed.  If the
+   cpufreq governor exists but /sys/kernel/hydrogenx is absent, boost controller
+   registration failed.
+5. vendor hooks are weak.  Missing MTK GPU/DDR symbols must not break a build.
+   The cpufreq/input path should still work.
+
+Runtime nodes
+-------------
+
+/sys/kernel/hydrogenx/version
+    Expected value: v10-audited-tree.
+
+/sys/kernel/hydrogenx/builtins
+    Prints the enabled bridge categories and confirms that the controller is
+    present in the running kernel.
+
+/sys/kernel/hydrogenx/status
+    Prints profile, game_mode, active boost pulses, floors, sched boost, uclamp
+    min, and whether input_hook is enabled.
+
+/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy*/scaling_available_governors
+    Must include hydrogenx.  If it does not, inspect dmesg for the registration
+    message from cpufreq_hydrogenx.c.
+
+Tuning philosophy
+-----------------
+
+The governor is intentionally not a pure performance lock.  It applies floors
+only when load, input, frame, game, or userspace scene signals justify the
+extra cost.  This is closer to an Android gaming kernel than a desktop
+performance governor: high short burst response, moderate sustained floor, and
+slow ramp-down to avoid oscillation.
+
+Profile: balanced
+-----------------
+
+Purpose: daily mixed UI, social apps, light gaming.
+
+Recommended baseline values::
+
+    echo 0 > /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/profile
+    echo 0 > /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/game_mode
+    echo 82 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/up_threshold
+    echo 32 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/down_threshold
+    echo 58 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/hispeed_load
+    echo 72 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/min_sample_time
+    echo 80 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/powersave_bias
+
+Expected behavior:
+
+* Up-ramp begins when smoothed load approaches 82 percent.
+* Hispeed floor appears around 58 percent load or during active scene pulses.
+* Down-ramp is delayed for about 72 ms to reduce oscillation.
+* Powersave bias value 80 keeps low-load frequency conservative.
+
+Profile: game
+-------------
+
+Purpose: games, emulators, recording, touch-heavy sessions.
+
+Recommended baseline values::
+
+    echo 1 > /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/profile
+    echo 1 > /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/game_mode
+    echo 72 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/up_threshold
+    echo 24 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/down_threshold
+    echo 45 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/hispeed_load
+    echo 90 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/min_sample_time
+    echo 0 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/powersave_bias
+
+Expected behavior:
+
+* Up-ramp begins when smoothed load approaches 72 percent.
+* Hispeed floor appears around 45 percent load or during active scene pulses.
+* Down-ramp is delayed for about 90 ms to reduce oscillation.
+* Powersave bias value 0 is disabled for maximum frame stability.
+
+Profile: battery
+----------------
+
+Purpose: standby, reading, background download, heat recovery.
+
+Recommended baseline values::
+
+    echo 2 > /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/profile
+    echo 0 > /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/game_mode
+    echo 90 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/up_threshold
+    echo 38 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/down_threshold
+    echo 72 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/hispeed_load
+    echo 120 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/min_sample_time
+    echo 180 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/hydrogenx/powersave_bias
+
+Expected behavior:
+
+* Up-ramp begins when smoothed load approaches 90 percent.
+* Hispeed floor appears around 72 percent load or during active scene pulses.
+* Down-ramp is delayed for about 120 ms to reduce oscillation.
+* Powersave bias value 180 keeps low-load frequency conservative.
+
+Verification case 01
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Command set::
+
+    echo hydrogenx > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_governor
+    echo 1 > /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/boostpulse
+    cat /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/status
+    cat /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_cur_freq
+
+Expected result:
+
+The available governors list contains hydrogenx, the active governor switches
+without EINVAL, status shows a nonzero generic boost window immediately after
+boostpulse, and scaling_cur_freq should rise toward the selected floor.  If the
+boost window appears but frequency does not move, the cpufreq driver or thermal
+limit is clamping the request.  If the boost window does not appear, the global
+controller did not initialize.  If hydrogenx is missing from the governor list,
+registration failed before policy init.
+
+Failure isolation:
+
+* Missing /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/version: CONFIG_HYDROGENX_BOOST was not built.
+* Missing governor only: inspect dmesg for cpufreq_register_governor errors.
+* Governor present but no per-policy tunables: cpufreq dbs attr setup failed.
+* Tunables present but no performance effect: thermal, MTK DVFS, or policy max
+  clamp is stronger than the governor request.
